  "title": "Zu Chongzhi",
  "summary": "A mathematician and astronomer born in Jiankang (now Nanjing). He bounded pi between 3.1415926 and 3.1415927 and gave 355/113 as its ratio, and proposed the Daming calendar in 462. Imperial ministers debated the calendar for two years and it was not adopted in his lifetime; MacTutor dates him 429-501.",
